:: Lab 1 (unavailable students)

(metadata:
"title", "Catching a Junior Apprentice",
"cardDesc", "Will they be able to help you?",
"img", "",
)

$cssColumnParent[

$cssColumnChild[
	$cssBox[
    	($funcImage: (passage: "S: Lab 1 (unavailable)")'s img)
         $cssBoxItem[''(print: (passage:)'s title )''<br>(print: (passage:)'s cardDesc)]
    ]
]

$cssColumnChild[

<!--randomize speaker based on $stuff's lighthouseDice (so that it only randomizes when clicking through a passage but not upon dipping in and out of menus)-->
(set: _speaker to (cond:
$stuff's lighthouseDice is 1, 1,
$stuff's lighthouseDice is 2, 2,
$stuff's lighthouseDice is 3, 3, 1
))
<!--enchant speaker lines-->
($funcNPCSpeakManual: "Student" + (str:_speaker))
<!--hook name-->
(set: _line to (hook: "Student" + (str:_speaker) + "Line"))


<!--content begins-->

<!--tracker A line-->
(cond:
$stuff's lighthouseTrackerA is 3, [{
You hail a group of students, and they immediately disperse, leaving the slowest or perhaps the boldest among them to face you down.
}],
$stuff's lighthouseTrackerA is 2, [{
Trying again, you catch up with another student. This one is carrying a heavy stack of books, who startled when at your approach, almost dropping the books and crushing your feet.
}],
$stuff's lighthouseTrackerA is 1, [{
Like an snakecat in ambush, you wait in a corner of the hallway, until you hear the footsteps. You appear, quicker than they can run. Well, quicker than at least one of them.
}],
)
<br>

<!--student reply-->
(cond:
_speaker is 1, [{
_line["(either: "Du-don't know. N-new to Apesai. A-ask big s-sister.", "Library? Lab? Bed? Teacher doesn't know? Then how would student know?", "Where is lab? Why? Ask big sister to get in.", "Is this school? Yes, it is school. There are classes, student must go.", "Ask the Nurandah people. Ask others. I will not help.",)"]
<br>
(either: "The student before you is a small child with terracotta skin - a native, one of many, and a little bit too young for school. One must wonder if the davehmars here are having a hard time finding readier students.", "His Nurango sentences are curt, utilitarian. You wonder if it is a pattern from his Askavan tongue, or if the native students actually speak in poetry when alone with one another.", "The apprentice keeps fixing her cap and gown, trying to get all of her thick, silver hair underneath the wraps, clearly unfamiliar with Nurandah clothing.")
<br>
}],
_speaker is 2, [{
_line["(either: "Erm, the lab? I'm not sure if I should... Who //are// you? I'm not sure strangers should be wandering around. You should talk to one of the teachers.", "Is this a school? Yes, it is. Why are you asking? Uh, listen, I better get to class. I'm already as late as it is.", "I just enrolled last month. I want to help, but truth is, I still ask the assistant where the washroom is, so...",)"]
<br>
(either: "The apprentice is wearing a blue-and-white sash - the colors of the Reclaimers. Her parents are probably living in a frontier settlement in the deserts to the north. She has it far better than them.", "This student is wearing a gold knife on one of his ears. Is he a Yavanid? Or is he merely copying the neighborhood minstrel? Hard to tell where tradition ends and fashion begins in a place as mixed as Apesai.", "With both black hair of Nurandah and copper skin of Askava, it is difficult to place this student's ethnicity. But perhaps the classic descriptions you've learned from textbooks have not accounted for centuries of co-existence.")
}],
_speaker is 3, [{
_line["(either: "Hmm? Why are you speaking to me? Shouldn't the adminstrators be handling new teachers? Excuse me.", "Oh, the school is a tower. There's only up and down. I'm sure if you keep climbing, you'll get to where you need to be. Now, if you'll excuse me, I also have somewhere I need to be.", "Tsk, I am a magus, not a tour guide. Of course I can call myself a 'magus'; I've already completed my basics. Now, if you'll excuse me...", "The school facilities... hm... I'm sure the assistant can help you. Yes, the //principal's// assistant. She's always around somewhere, if not the market.",)"]
<br>
(either: "You didn't expect to hear the Sanurango accent in this place, which this student is definitely trying to exaggerate. Aristocrats are the same anywhere - they cannot help themselves.", "The apprentice's gown is so fine that you wonder if it is breaking some kind of dress code. But then again, rules often bend around those whose parents can afford them such nice clothes.", "Black hair, fair skin, this apprentice is unmistakably Nurandahid. After being surrounded by foreigners, the sight of an imperial comes as a shock to you.")
}],
)
<br>

<!--another tracker A line-->
(cond:
$stuff's lighthouseTrackerA is 3, [{
4->3
}],
$stuff's lighthouseTrackerA is 2, [{
3->2
}],
$stuff's lighthouseTrackerA is 1, [{
2->1
}],
)
<br>

<!--content ends-->



---
<!--run code for dynamic choices, using $stuff as tracker-->
(display: "code.lighthouseUnavailableChoices")

]<!--end child-->
]<!--end parent-->